# DevOps.Scanner.SDK local config — TEMPLATE (tracked in git).
#
# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in values:
#     cp .env.template .env
#
# This root .env is a MINIMAL BOOTSTRAP — DATA_DIR only. Once DATA_DIR is
# known, scripts/lib/load-env.sh additionally (and optionally) sources, in
# order, later overriding earlier:
#   1. $DATA_DIR/config/common/.env              cross-repo shared values
#                                                 (shared with sibling repos
#                                                 like DevOps.Inventory and
#                                                 DevOps.External.Attack.Surface,
#                                                 defined in exactly one place)
#   2. $DATA_DIR/config/DevOps.Scanner.SDK/.env   this repo's own overrides,
#                                                 if any
# Both are outside this repo's git-synced mount and entirely optional —
# missing files mean today's (unchanged) behavior. This repo has no scripts
# that need DATA_DIR today; scripts/lib/load-env.sh is provided so any future
# host-side script (or scripts/setup.sh) can adopt the same cascade instead
# of duplicating it.

# --- Host data root (optional; only needed if/when a script here sources
# scripts/lib/load-env.sh) --------------------------------------------------
# DATA_DIR=/data/VulnScanData

# --- Docs-tooling only (read directly by scripts/gen-badges.sh; NOT part of
# the cascade above — see that script for details) --------------------------
# AZURE_DEVOPS_ORG=<your-org>
# AZURE_DEVOPS_PROJECT=<your-project>
# AZURE_DEVOPS_BADGE_LIVE=true
# PYTHON_VERSION=3.14

# --- Everything else lives under $DATA_DIR/config/ -------------------------
# Any other optional setting belongs in $DATA_DIR/config/common/.env (shared
# across DevOps.* repos) or $DATA_DIR/config/DevOps.Scanner.SDK/.env (this
# repo only) — see the .env.template in each of those directories for the
# full list and explanations. Nothing else belongs in this root file.
